## Background content ## {#background-content}

## <dfn id="dfn-content-scripts">Content scripts</dfn> ## {#content-scripts}

Content scripts represent a set of JS and CSS files that should be injected into matching pages loaded by the user agent. They are injected using the [=inject a content script=] algorithm. Content scripts run in an [=isolated world=] by default.

Each item of the {{WebExtensionManifest/content_scripts}} key is described by the {{ManifestContentScript}} dictionary:

<xmp class="idl" noexport>
dictionary ManifestContentScript {
  required sequence<DOMString> matches;
  sequence<DOMString> exclude_matches;
  sequence<DOMString> js;
  sequence<DOMString> css;
  boolean all_frames = false;
  boolean match_about_blank = false;
  boolean match_origin_as_fallback = false;
  RunAt run_at;
  sequence<DOMString> include_globs;
  sequence<DOMString> exclude_globs;
  ExecutionWorld world = "ISOLATED";
};
</xmp>

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>matches</dfn> ### {#key-content_scripts-matches}

A [=list=] of [=match patterns=] that are used to decide which pages the user agent injects the content script into. This key is required.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>exclude_matches</dfn> ### {#key-exclude_matches}

A [=list=] of [=match patterns=] that can be used to specify URLs where the content script should not run, even if the URL matches entries in {{ManifestContentScript/matches}} and (if specified) {{ManifestContentScript/include_globs}}.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>js</dfn> ### {#key-js}

A [=list=] of file paths, relative to the extension's package, that should be injected as scripts.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>css</dfn> ### {#key-css}

A [=list=] of file paths, relative to the extension's package, that should be injected as stylesheets.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>all_frames</dfn> ### {#key-all_frames}

If `all_frames` is `true`, the content script must be injected into any subframes that match the other matching criteria for the content script. If `false`, content scripts will only be injected into top-level documents. Defaults to `false`.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>match_about_blank</dfn> ### {#key-match_about_blank}

If this is `true`, use the URL of the parent frame when matching a child frame whose document URL is `about:blank` or `about:srcdoc`. See also [=determine the URL for matching a document=]. Defaults to `false`.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>match_origin_as_fallback</dfn> ### {#key-match_origin_as_fallback}

If this is `true`, use fallbacks as described in [=determine the URL for matching a document=].

No path is available when the URL to match against falls back to an origin. Therefore, when set, the user agent may treat a {{ManifestContentScript/matches}} with a path other than `/*` as an error.

Defaults to `false`.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>run_at</dfn> ### {#key-run_at}

Specifies when the content script should be injected. Valid values are defined by the {{RunAt}} enum.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>include_globs</dfn> ### {#key-include_globs}

A list of [=globs=] that a document should match. A document matches if the URL matches both the {{ManifestContentScript/matches}} field and the {{ManifestContentScript/include_globs}} field.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>exclude_globs</dfn> ### {#key-exclude_globs}

A [=list=] of [=globs=] that can be used to specify URLs where the content script should not run, even if the URL matches entries in {{ManifestContentScript/matches}} and (if specified) {{ManifestContentScript/include_globs}}.

### Key <dfn dict-member for=ManifestContentScript noexport>world</dfn> ### {#key-world}

The [=world=] any JavaScript scripts should be injected into. Defaults to `ISOLATED`. Valid values are defined by the {{ExecutionWorld}} enum.

### `RunAt` enum ### {#runat-enum}

<pre class="idl">
enum RunAt {
    "document_start",
    "document_end",
    "document_idle"
};
</pre>

The {{RunAt}} enum represents when a content script should be injected.

### `ExecutionWorld` enum ### {#executionworld-enum}

<pre class="idl">
enum ExecutionWorld {
    "ISOLATED",
    "MAIN"
};
</pre>

The {{ExecutionWorld}} enum represents a JavaScript [=world=].

"ISOLATED" corresponds to an [=isolated world=].

"MAIN" corresponds to the [=main world=].

