## Determine the URL for matching a document ## {#determine-the-url-for-matching-a-document}

<div algorithm>
To <dfn id="dfn-determine-the-url-for-matching-a-document">determine the URL for matching a document</dfn>, given a [=/document=] |document|, a boolean |matchOriginAsFallback| and a boolean |matchAboutBlank|:

1. Let |url| be |document|'s [=Document/URL=].
1. If |url|'s [=url/scheme=] is "`http`", "`https`" or "`file`", return |url|.
1. If |url|'s [=url/scheme=] is "`blob`", "`data`" or "`filesystem`", or if |url| is "`about:blank`" or "`about:srcdoc`":
    1. If |matchOriginAsFallback| is true:
        1. Let |origin| be |document|'s [=Document/origin=].
        1. If |origin| is a [=tuple origin=]:
            1. If |origin|'s <l spec=html>[=origin/scheme=]</l> is "`http`", "`https`" or "`file`", return the [=serialization of an origin|serialization=] of |origin|.
            1. Return null.
        1. Otherwise, |origin| is an [=opaque origin=]:
            1. Let |precursorOrigin| be |document|'s precursor origin, if any.

                Issue: "precursor origin" concept needs to be specified. It is not in the HTML spec at the moment. At least Chrome and Firefox recognize the concept, see e.g. https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1715167.
            1. If |precursorOrigin| is a [=tuple origin=] and its <l spec=html>[=origin/scheme=]</l> is "`http`", "`https`" or "`file`", return the [=serialization of an origin|serialization=] of |precursorOrigin|.
            1. Return null.
    1. Otherwise, if |matchAboutBlank| is true and |url| is "`about:blank`" or "`about:srcdoc`":
        1. Let |opener| be the [=active document=] of |document|'s [=opener browsing context=].
        1. If all of the following conditions are true:
            - |opener| is not null
            - |opener|'s [=Document/origin=] is still the same as |document|'s <l spec=html>[=opener origin at creation=]</l>
            - This algorithm has not already been run for |opener| while determining the URL for |document|.

            Then return the result of running [=determine the URL for matching a document=] given |opener|, |matchOriginAsFallback| and |matchAboutBlank|.
1. Return null.

</div>

## Inject a content script ## {#inject-a-content-script}

Issue: If the same extension specifies the same script twice, what should happen? ([bug](https://crbug.com/324096753))

<div algorithm>
To <dfn id="dfn-inject-a-content-script">inject a content script</dfn>, given a {{ManifestContentScript}} |script| and a [=/document=] |document|:

1. Let |url| be the result of running [=determine the URL for matching a document=] given |document|, |script|["{{ManifestContentScript/match_origin_as_fallback}}"] and |script|["{{ManifestContentScript/match_about_blank}}"].
1. If |url| is null, return.
1. If the extension does not have access to |url|, return.
1. If |url| is not matched by any [=match pattern=] in |script|["{{ManifestContentScript/matches}}"], return.
1. If |script|["{{ManifestContentScript/include_globs}}"] [=map/exists=] and |url| is not matched by any [=glob=] in it, return.
1. If |url| is matched by any entry in |script|["{{ManifestContentScript/exclude_matches}}"] or |script|["{{ManifestContentScript/exclude_globs}}"], return.
1. If |document| is in a child frame and |script|["{{ManifestContentScript/all_frames}}"] is false, return.
1. Inject the content script into |document|, at the time indicated by |script|["{{ManifestContentScript/run_at}}"].

</div>

